From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] directmanipulation: a window subclassed after us keeps us in its chain, not subclassed twice (9557)

Activate subclasses the window to see its pointer messages and timer
(1668); Deactivate, or the manager's release, restored the old
procedure only if ours was still the window's -- and forgot the window
either way. When the program had subclassed the window after us, its
procedure kept calling ours as its previous one; a later Activate (a
new manager for the same window) then subclassed the window again,
taking the program's procedure as our previous one. Ours called the
program's, the program's called ours, and the first message went round
until the stack ran out.

Steam's web helper (Chromium 126, whose touchpad support activates and
deactivates Direct Manipulation on its windows) subclasses its windows
after it: the helper died of the stack overflow every few seconds as
its sign-in window came up, Steam restarted it ("Restart webhelper
process, counter 2"), and Steam never showed a window.

Now a window we cannot take ourselves out of keeps its record, idle,
passing every message on; an Activate for it uses the record instead of
subclassing again; the record goes with the window (WM_NCDESTROY).

Gate: test/dmsubclass-gate.sh. Mutant SG_MUTANT_DM_SUBCLASS_FORGOTTEN
(directmanipulation/directmanipulation.c).
---
diff --git a/dlls/directmanipulation/directmanipulation.c b/dlls/directmanipulation/directmanipulation.c
--- a/dlls/directmanipulation/directmanipulation.c
+++ b/dlls/directmanipulation/directmanipulation.c
@@ -719,6 +719,24 @@ static LRESULT CALLBACK subclass_proc( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam, LPARA
     }
     LeaveCriticalSection( &dm_cs );
     if (!old) return DefWindowProcW( hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DM_SUBCLASS_FORGOTTEN
+    if (msg == WM_NCDESTROY)
+    {
+        /* the window goes: so does what we kept of it (9557) */
+        LRESULT ret = CallWindowProcW( old, hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam );
+        EnterCriticalSection( &dm_cs );
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( sc, &subclassed_windows, struct subclassed, entry )
+        {
+            if (sc->window != hwnd) continue;
+            list_remove( &sc->entry );
+            free( sc );
+            break;
+        }
+        LeaveCriticalSection( &dm_cs );
+        for (i = 0; i < n; i++) IDirectManipulationManager2_Release( &managers[i]->IDirectManipulationManager2_iface );
+        return ret;
+    }
+#endif
 
     if (msg == WM_TIMER && wparam == TIMER_ID)
     {
@@ -2005,11 +2023,27 @@ static void unsubclass( HWND window )
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( sc, &subclassed_windows, struct subclassed, entry )
     {
         if (sc->window != window) continue;
-        if (--sc->refs) return;
+        if (!sc->refs || --sc->refs) return;
         if (IsWindow( window ) && (WNDPROC)GetWindowLongPtrW( window, GWLP_WNDPROC ) == subclass_proc)
+        {
             SetWindowLongPtrW( window, GWLP_WNDPROC, (LONG_PTR)sc->old_proc );
-        list_remove( &sc->entry );
-        free( sc );
+            list_remove( &sc->entry );
+            free( sc );
+        }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DM_SUBCLASS_FORGOTTEN
+        /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9557): the window was subclassed again
+         * after us (Steam's web helper does it to its windows): whoever did
+         * calls us as its previous procedure, so we stay in its chain, idle,
+         * passing everything on -- forgotten, a later Activate subclassed the
+         * window once more, our previous procedure became theirs, theirs was
+         * us, and the first message went round until the stack ran out */
+        else if (IsWindow( window )) ;
+#endif
+        else
+        {
+            list_remove( &sc->entry );
+            free( sc );
+        }
         return;
     }
 }
@@ -2067,6 +2101,8 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI direct_manip_Activate( IDirectManipulationManager2 *iface,
     list_add_tail( &This->windows, &w->entry );
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( sc, &subclassed_windows, struct subclassed, entry )
         if (sc->window == window) break;
+    /* (9557) a window we are still in the chain of -- kept, idle, after the last
+     * Deactivate -- is not subclassed a second time */
     if (&sc->entry != &subclassed_windows) sc->refs++;
     else if ((sc = calloc( 1, sizeof(*sc) )))
     {
